+### [Non-Linear Sphere Tracing](4079-non-linear-sphere-tracing.md)
+Non-Linear Sphere Tracing (NLST) is a rendering method for directly visualizing deformed Signed Distance Fields (SDFs) without converting them to explicit meshes. It solves the incompatibility between standard sphere tracing and non-linear deformation techniques (such as Linear Blend Skinning or Free-Form Deformations), which invalidate the Euclidean distance metric required for safe stepping. Unlike meshing approaches like Marching Cubes, NLST maintains infinite resolution and sharp features, and unlike methods requiring inverse deformations, it works with general forward deformation functions by integrating the ray path as a curve in object space.
